 -- Antonio Morales García <info@kidux.org>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:31:29 +0200

kidux-daemon (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Access control and time: unlimited, daily and manual modes, a bank of
    granted time, the day changing at four in the morning and never going
    backwards, warnings at ten, five and one minute.
  * Sessions are learnt from logind and counted by the daemon, so nothing a
    child runs can stop the clock.
  * The lock: a lock screen on its own terminal, the seat switched to it, the
    child's session frozen underneath; the session is ended instead if logind
    does not confirm the switch.
  * An adult can give more time, unlock briefly so the child can save, or log
    the child out; the child can continue with their own password.
  * The power button and Ctrl+Alt+Escape always bring up a trusted screen.

 -- Antonio Morales García <info@kidux.org>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 23:05:45 +0200

kidux-daemon (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Depend on perl: deluser needs it to remove a child's home directory, and
    without it deleting a child fails on a minimal installation.

 -- Antonio Morales García <info@kidux.org>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:52:09 +0200

kidux-daemon (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the one privileged process in Kidux.
  * The adult password, stored as an argon2id hash, and adult-panel tokens
    bound to the connection that unlocked.
  * Children: create, delete, change their profile and password.
  * polkit actions and rules deciding who may call what, and the daemon's
    own checks on which child a call may touch.
  * First boot: the state directory, the GRUB recovery password, and every
    administrator made an adult of the family's state.

 -- Antonio Morales García <info@kidux.org>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:46:30 +0200
